::SPEECH_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.02
Question:
Point: Rehearsal improves timing. Which support best fits?
{
~A. Speeches can happen in classrooms.#This is related to speaking but does not explain timing.
~B. Timing is a word.#This does not support the speech point.
~C. Some students like posters.#This is unrelated to rehearsal and timing.
=D. A speaker can time each section during practice and revise sections that run too long.#Correct. This support directly explains how rehearsal improves timing.
}
::SPEECH_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q02::
Question ID: SPEECH_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.SPK.01
Question:
Which transition is most purposeful?
{
~A. Next thing.#This is vague and does not show the relationship between ideas.
~B. I am done with that.#This announces stopping but does not connect ideas.
=C. After rehearsal helps control timing, organized notes help guide delivery.#Correct. This transition connects two preparation ideas.
~D. Whatever comes after.#This is informal and unclear.
}
::SPEECH_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q03::
Question ID: SPEECH_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.02
Question:
Which sentence gives reasoning?
{
=A. This support matters because organized notes keep the speaker from skipping a main point.#Correct. This explains why the support helps.
~B. Organized notes exist.#This is a detail but does not explain why it matters.
~C. My next point is coming.#This is a transition, not reasoning.
~D. Notes are notes.#This repeats wording without explanation.
}
::SPEECH_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q04::
Question ID: SPEECH_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.PRES.02
Question:
Which speech note is most useful for format and delivery?
{
~A. Say stuff.#This is too vague for quality speech notes.
=B. Point 1: note cards list main points; explain order.#Correct. This note gives a clear format cue and speaking reminder.
~C. Everything maybe.#This does not guide the speaker.
~D. Read all paragraphs.#This may prevent natural delivery.
}
::SPEECH_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q05::
Question ID: SPEECH_U02_L06_GuidedPractice_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.02
Question:
Which support is too general?
{
~A. A timer can show whether the introduction takes one minute.#This is specific support.
~B. A note card can list the three main points in order.#This is specific support.
=C. Practice is good.#Correct. This is too general because it does not explain how practice helps.
~D. A chart can show changes over time.#This is a specific support detail.
}
